Title:
Cruising Forward with the Tradecraft Garden

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This post announces a new release of Tradecraft Garden / Crystal Palace, focusing on usability and new low-level tradecraft features for position-independent loaders and tooling.  
- It consolidates multiple prior commands into a single `cpl [verb] [args]` CLI, adds an install script, and provides optional bash tab completion to streamline workflows.  
- A new x64-only linker intrinsic `__transfer()` is introduced to force a tail-call style control transfer at link time, removing the loader from the call stack to reduce stack artifacts.  
- The release expands dynamic API resolution to support additional hashing contracts (djb2, fnv1a, sdbm) beyond ror13, with examples demonstrating alternate hashing in a simple PIC loader.  
- Migration notes cover spec/import changes for BOF workflows and a behavioral change in `findFunctionByHash` handling forwarded exports via `GetProcAddress`, including guidance when using `__resolve_hook`.  
- Useful for red team operators, implant/tooling developers, and researchers building PIC loaders/BOFs who care about call stack hygiene and flexible API resolution.

Technical Focus:
- CLI/tooling consolidation (`cpl` verbs) and install automation
- x64 tail-call control transfer via linker intrinsic (`__transfer`)
- Dynamic Function Resolution (DFR) and Win32 API hashing contracts (ror13, djb2, fnv1a, sdbm)
- COFF parsing/disassembly and PIC linking/build pipeline
- Forwarded export handling and `GetProcAddress` interactions
- Stack safety considerations (SEH/unwind metadata) in PIC contexts

Use Cases:
- Standardize and script Crystal Palace workflows via a single `cpl` entry point
- Build/link PIC DLL loaders and BOF-related artifacts from `.spec` files
- Reduce loader visibility in call stacks using tail-call transfer semantics
- Swap API hashing algorithms to vary static signatures and resolver behavior
- Debug/avoid resolver-hook side effects when mixing `__resolve_hook`, `dprintf`, and `GetProcAddress`

Keywords:
Tradecraft Garden, Crystal Palace, cpl CLI, position-independent code, PIC loader, COFF, disassembly, linker intrinsic, __transfer, tail call, call stack evasion, Dynamic Function Resolution, API hashing, ror13, djb2, fnv1a, sdbm, GetProcAddress, forwarded exports, BOF, BeaconOutput, __resolve_hook, OutputDebugStringA, SEH, x64 unwind metadata